  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      84.62,
      551.73,
      519.74,
      567.87
    ],
    "text": "The cause of action disclosed by the plaintiff is on the basis of constructive malicious",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.07893180847168,
      12.100000381469727,
      12.444350242614746
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      48.84,
      579.33,
      519.66,
      595.47
    ],
    "text": "desertion on the part of the defendant. Such a cause of action is recognized in our law under",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.100000381469727,
      12.444350242614746
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      48.98,
      606.94,
      518.83,
      623.08
    ],
    "text": "Section 19(2) of the Marriage (General) Ordinance. Hence, it is the burden of the plaintiff to",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.05275821685791,
      12.100000381469727,
      12.444350242614746
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      48.59,
      634.77,
      519.16,
      650.91
    ],
    "text": "establish that the acts of the defendant compelled him to leave the matrimonial home. In this",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.024515151977539,
      12.100000381469727,
      12.444350242614746
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      48.61,
      662.37,
      518.47,
      678.51
    ],
    "text": "instance, the plaintiff alleged that the cruelty on the part of the defendant had been the reason for",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.075825691223145,
      12.100000381469727,
      12.444350242614746
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      284.35,
      31.59,
      293.12,
      47.2
    ],
    "text": "4",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.699999809265137
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      53.74,
      67.86,
      524.12,
      83.73
    ],
    "text": "him to leave her. In such a situation, alleged cruelty should have been caused deliberately by the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.790092468261719,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      53.66,
      95.23,
      326.52,
      111.1
    ],
    "text": "defendant with the intention of repudiating the marriage.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      88.71,
      150.67,
      524.4,
      166.55
    ],
    "text": "In this regard, Hahlo in the book titled \"The South African Law of Husband and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      11.903249740600586,
      11.972280502319336,
      11.976553916931152,
      12.005135536193848,
      12.06983757019043
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      53.0,
      178.02,
      279.58,
      193.89
    ],
    "text": "Wife\" [Second Edition at Pg.382) states thus:",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.268882751464844
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      89.98,
      221.33,
      423.14,
      235.74
    ],
    "text": "\"Any form of cruelty or neglect which is sufficient to found an action",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.800000190734863,
      13.114035606384277
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      92.54,
      241.98,
      434.87,
      256.39
    ],
    "text": "for judicial separation is also sufficient to found an action for divorce,",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.76284122467041,
      11.770513534545898,
      11.800000190734863,
      11.828315734863281
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.98,
      262.85,
      436.04,
      277.27
    ],
    "text": "on the ground of constructive desertion, provided the defendant acted",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.800000190734863,
      13.114035606384277
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      94.26,
      282.28,
      396.82,
      298.03
    ],
    "text": "with the intention to put an end to the marital relationship. \"",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.800000190734863,
      11.940217018127441,
      12.225624084472656
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      88.0,
      323.22,
      523.02,
      339.09
    ],
    "text": "In the case ofV.R.Sinnathamby V Annammah [55 N.L.R. at page 349] many disputes",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      11.940629959106445,
      11.942523956298828,
      12.268882751464844
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      52.81,
      351.3,
      523.16,
      367.18
    ],
    "text": "between a husband and his wife had erupted because the wife insisted that her brother should",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      52.55,
      378.91,
      523.05,
      394.79
    ],
    "text": "remain in the house contrary to the desire of the husband. There was evidence that the husband",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      52.3,
      406.26,
      522.66,
      422.13
    ],
    "text": "was assaulted on two occasions by the wife's brother and that, on the second occasion, the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      52.28,
      433.85,
      522.76,
      449.73
    ],
    "text": "husband left the home. In that decision it was held that under those circumstances the husband's",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      52.19,
      461.94,
      358.38,
      477.81
    ],
    "text": "departure from the home did not constitute malicious desertion.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      87.46,
      516.65,
      540.2,
      532.53
    ],
    "text": "The evidence in this case, as to the circumstances that led for the plaintiff to leave the home",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      52.18,
      544.5,
      537.14,
      560.41
    ],
    "text": "does not even so grave. It seems that basically it is on the strength of the evidence as to the non-",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.88669204711914,
      11.899999618530273,
      12.171957969665527,
      12.474531173706055
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      51.98,
      572.35,
      540.66,
      588.22
    ],
    "text": "disclosure of a child been born to the defendant that the plaintiff sought to have a divorce. All that",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      51.93,
      600.18,
      540.51,
      616.06
    ],
    "text": "evidence has been considered by the learned District Judge and has decided that no sufficient",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      51.69,
      627.54,
      540.06,
      643.42
    ],
    "text": "evidence is forthcoming to establish constructive malicious desertion. He being the trial judge is the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      51.85,
      655.15,
      539.39,
      671.02
    ],
    "text": "best person to decide whether the defendant intended to bring the matrimonial relationship to an end.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      285.2,
      32.49,
      293.68,
      47.57
    ],
    "text": "5",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.300000190734863
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      54.86,
      67.38,
      543.06,
      83.87
    ],
    "text": "This position was upheld in the case ofP.P.Wickremasuriya V S.L.S.R.Samarasuriya. [68 N.L.R.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      55.31,
      95.47,
      287.91,
      111.96
    ],
    "text": "(1965) at page 349] In that decision it was held:",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      92.18,
      136.47,
      489.28,
      152.08
    ],
    "text": "\" The findings of the learned Judge were reached after having had the advantage -",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.617257118225098,
      11.699999809265137,
      11.761885643005371,
      12.924385070800781
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      90.43,
      157.12,
      506.38,
      172.73
    ],
    "text": "denied to Appellate Courts - of seeing and hearing the parties. It was for the learned",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.699999809265137,
      11.732405662536621,
      12.924385070800781
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      90.12,
      178.95,
      516.31,
      193.24
    ],
    "text": "Judge to decide whether the husband's conduct towards his wife caused her to leave: it",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.699999809265137
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      90.42,
      199.58,
      519.67,
      213.87
    ],
    "text": "was for the learned Judge to decide all such questions of knowledge and intention on his",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.699999809265137,
      11.807356834411621,
      13.058348655700684
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      89.43,
      220.95,
      363.09,
      235.24
    ],
    "text": "part as would show whether he was guilty of desertion\".",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.699999809265137,
      12.924385070800781
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      126.18,
      260.11,
      525.97,
      275.98
    ],
    "text": "Having considered the circumstances of this case, it is my considered view that",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.206210136413574
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      55.42,
      287.69,
      526.37,
      303.57
    ],
    "text": "the learned District Judge is correct when he decided that the plaintiff has failed to establish",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      55.6,
      315.54,
      526.1,
      331.42
    ],
    "text": "constructive malicious desertion on the part of the defendant. Moreover, as decided in",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.206210136413574
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      55.87,
      342.91,
      525.61,
      358.78
    ],
    "text": "Wickramasuriya V Samarasuriya (supra) this Court exercising appellate powers does not wish to",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      56.06,
      370.75,
      526.45,
      386.63
    ],
    "text": "interfere with the findings arrived at by the trial judge on the facts of the case since no glaring",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      55.9,
      398.58,
      526.15,
      414.46
    ],
    "text": "mistake is found therein. In the circumstances, I do not see any reason to interfere with the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.804718971252441,
      11.849493026733398,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      56.03,
      426.42,
      427.36,
      442.3
    ],
    "text": "findings of the learned District Judge. Accordingly, this appeal is dismissed.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.206210136413574
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      56.35,
      472.02,
      514.35,
      487.89
    ],
    "text": "Having considered the circumstances of this case, I make no order as to the costs of the appeal.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      56.1,
      521.9,
      142.72,
      536.19
    ],
    "text": "Appeal dismissed.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.699999809265137
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      236.09,
      600.42,
      432.79,
      616.29
    ],
    "text": "JUDGE OF THE COURT OF APPEAL",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.847935676574707,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  }
]